                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "745c39dd-468d-4670-b106-d30333635d71",
                                "sense_id": "d3ba446d-82b9-3cd7-ac6f-7b406b6197a3",
                                "text": "Then light and swift through the jungle trees / We swung in our airy flights, / Or breathed in the balms of the fronded palms / In the hush of the moonless nights;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86435932-c17c-4d0f-af43-b79223af67ee",
                                "sense_id": "d3ba446d-82b9-3cd7-ac6f-7b406b6197a3",
                                "text": "1912, John Muir, The Yosemite, Chapter 5: The Trees of the Valley,\nThe branches, outspread in flat plumes and, beautifully fronded, sweep gracefully downward and outward, […] ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d529402-d8b9-4990-943b-974f27e80341",
                                "sense_id": "d3ba446d-82b9-3cd7-ac6f-7b406b6197a3",
                                "text": "1966, Malacological Society of Australia, Malacological Society of Australia, Issues 1-10, page 27,\nOn the other hand there is in the author's collection a specimen with single nodules only from 40 fathoms off Wollongong, but more fronded than most shore dwelling forms, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49f14c24-855b-4d91-b66a-1e7e503db18c",
                                "sense_id": "d3ba446d-82b9-3cd7-ac6f-7b406b6197a3",
                                "text": "Headaches, as well as the unease consequent upon bad dreams, can be relieved by making a fronded stick with a rudimentary face (butun); the pain, or the inauspiciousness, is transferred to this stick, which is left in the forest, […]"
                            }
